From: Foundry <hi@m7.rs>
Subject: [PATCH] use Generic OAuth picture claims for user avatars

Persist a valid HTTPS picture URL at login and hotlink it from the existing
SQL-backed user views, falling back to the existing Gravatar behavior.
No image downloader, proxy, or provider refresh is involved.

diff --git a/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/generic-oauth/profile-pictures.md b/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/generic-oauth/profile-pictures.md
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/generic-oauth/profile-pictures.md
@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+---
+title: OIDC profile pictures
+description: Use Generic OAuth picture claims as profile images
+---
+
+# OIDC profile pictures
+
+Generic OAuth reads the standard `picture` claim using its existing source
+precedence: ID token, UserInfo, then access token. The first valid absolute
+HTTPS URL wins. Missing, non-string, insecure, credential-bearing, or oversized
+URLs are ignored. No additional Grafana setting is required.
+
+The URL is persisted on the SQL-backed user at login and used in the sidebar,
+user profiles, user and team-member lists, permissions, and annotations. A
+subsequent Generic OAuth login updates it, or clears it if no valid picture
+is supplied. Other login methods do not clear it. Existing users get their
+picture on their next OAuth login; this does not force existing sessions out.
+
+The browser hotlinks the image. Grafana neither downloads nor proxies it, and
+normal dashboard requests do not contact the identity provider for a new URL.
+Image hosts must be allowed by any custom Content Security Policy. They see
+the browser's image requests, and the URL must work without a Grafana access
+token. A valid URL that later fails to load does not automatically fall back.
+
+Without a valid picture, the existing Gravatar behavior is unchanged: Gravatar
+when enabled, otherwise the default profile image. Disabling Gravatar does not
+disable OIDC pictures. Team and service-account avatars are unchanged.
+
+Authentik's stock `profile` scope already emits URL avatars as `picture` and
+omits inline `data:` avatars. No custom mapping is needed for absolute HTTPS
+URLs. Request the `profile` scope as usual. Providers emitting relative URLs
+must first convert those to absolute HTTPS URLs in their scope mapping.
+
+This patch targets Grafana's SQL-backed users, not the experimental Kubernetes
+user service or IAM identity-display APIs.
